<title>MAURITIUS: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MAURITIUS GOVERNMENT LIST (970621)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  * 21 Jun 97 - The Mauritian Militant Movement quit its    *</p>
<p>  *		 alliance with the Labour Party and left     *</p>
<p>  *		 the government. MMM leader Paul Berenger    *</p>
<p>  *		 was relieved of his post of deputy PM and   *</p>
<p>  *		 foreign minister, the latter job taken over *</p>
<p>  *		 by PM Ramgoolam.				    *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>President (took office 1 Jul 92)..Cassam UTEEM</p>
<p>Vice President</p>
<p>    (took office 1 Jul 92).........Sir Rabindranath GHURBURRUN</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT (Approved 30 Dec 95; Reshuffled 27 Nov 96)</p>
<p>Prime Minister..Navin RAMGOOLAM</p>
<p>(also Minister for Defence &amp; Home Affairs, Foreign</p>
<p>Affairs External Communications &amp; Information</p>
<p>Technology, Rodrigues &amp; Outer Islands)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Natural Resources..Arvin BOOLELL</p>
<p> Arts, Culture &amp; Leisure.......Dhurma Gian NATH</p>
<p> Attorney General, Justice, Human Rights &amp;</p>
<p>    Corporate Affairs......Abdool Razack PEEROO</p>
<p> Civil Service Affairs............Tsang Fan Hin TSANG MANG KIN</p>
<p> Defence &amp; Home Affairs......See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Economic Planning, International Trade &amp;</p>
<p> Telecommunications........Rajkeswur PURRYAG</p>
<p> Education, Science &amp; Technology.............James Burty DAVID</p>
<p> Environment &amp; Quality of Life...Rajesh BHAGWAN</p>
<p> External Communications &amp; Information......See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Finance.........Vasant BUNWAREE</p>
<p> Fisheries, Cooperatives &amp;</p>
<p> Marine Resource Development...Motee RAMDASS</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs.............See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Health...Ramsamy Kadress PILLAY</p>
<p> Housing &amp; Land Development..........Alan GANOO</p>
<p> Human Resource Development &amp;</p>
<p> Reform Institutions.....Samioullah LAUTHAN</p>
<p> Industry &amp; Commerce.......Jayakrishna CUTTAREE</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Industrial Relations..........Louis Steven OBEEGADOO</p>
<p> Land Transport, Shipping &amp;</p>
<p>    Public Safety ......Ahmed Rashid BEEBEEJAUN</p>
<p> Local Government &amp; Public Utilities.......Devanand VIRAHSAWMY</p>
<p> Public Infrastructure...Siddick Mohummud CHADY</p>
<p> Rodrigues &amp; Outer Islands...See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Social Solidarity &amp;</p>
<p> National Solidarity..Marie Joceline MINERVE</p>
<p> Tourism.........Jose ARUNASALON</p>
<p> Women, Family Welfare &amp;</p>
<p> Child Development.....Indira THACOOR-SIDAYA</p>
<p> Youth &amp; Sports.......Sachindev Kumar SOONARANE</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Parliament Speaker.......Sir Ramesh JEEWOOLALL</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor...............Dan MARAYE</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
